comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-25T15:20:06.567Z","harness:claude-code","Scope from the PR #1782 review (Codex round 8): besides the resolution kind, record which npm registry a freshness check used. pm package manage runs npm view from the caller's working directory, so with --pm-path from another directory a project .npmrc registry is not applied, and the observation can store the wrong registry's version. Resolve the registry from the tracker's workspace (or record it at install time) and use it for live checks and upgrades."
  "2026-11-25T22:39:58.258Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 15 on PR #1782 repeated this: npm:<name> that resolved to a local directory is classified as a registry source by isRegistryNpmSource, so manage can record an unrelated registry version as an update; record the installer's resolved provenance and use it for freshness and upgrade."
  "2026-11-26T00:54:08.727Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 17 on PR #1782: once install provenance is recorded, bind the update-observation identity to it too (installed GitHub commit or resolved npm package and version), so a reinstall that keeps manifest_version and updated_at (two pinned-clock runs) retires an earlier observation."
  "2026-11-26T03:56:26.453Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 20 on PR #1782: pm package upgrade replays a relative artifact spec such as npm:artifacts/demo.tgz against the caller's working directory, which can differ from the install's when --pm-path points elsewhere (main already replays local specs this way); record a stable artifact location at install time and refuse ambiguous legacy relative paths."
  "2026-11-26T04:35:19.023Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 21 on PR #1782: once the installed source revision is recorded, store the full remote commit in the observation and validate a GitHub verdict, negative included, against the installed commit with checkGithubUpdate's comparison, shortening the hash only for display."
body: ""
